
# 12. Bucket Sort

## Question Description
Implement the Bucket Sort algorithm in C++ to sort an array of floating-point numbers in ascending order. The algorithm distributes elements into buckets, sorts each bucket, and combines them.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[0.42, 0.32, 0.23, 0.52, 0.25, 0.47, 0.51]`

Expected Output:
`[0.23, 0.25, 0.32, 0.42, 0.47, 0.51, 0.52]`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[0.8, 0.4, 0.2, 0.6]`

Expected Output:
`[0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8]`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[0.5, 0.1, 0.9]`

Expected Output:
`[0.1, 0.5, 0.9]`

## Time Complexity
- Average Case: O(n + k), under suitable distribution assumptions
- Worst Case: O(n²), depending on bucket distribution and sorting method

## Space Complexity
- O(n + k), where k is the number of buckets.
